WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.080
"How to Keep Your Microbiome
Healthy with Prebiotic Foods"

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.280
If you look at the classics, the
most frequently cited articles

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.920
in the scientific nutrition&nbsp;
literature, the original

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:20.800
glycemic index paper comes out
at #10, cited over a thousand times.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.080
Learning about fruit, vegetables, and
cancer prevention was a hallmark.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.160
But hitting the top 5,
cited more than 2,000 times,

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.200
“Dietary modulation of
the human microbiom

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.200
introducing the concept of prebiotics.”

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.920
Prebiotics are the food
components that feed and nourish

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.920
the good bacteria in our gut,
like fiber and resistant starch.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.480
In general, eating
high-fiber plant foods is

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.280
a good foundation for
a prebiotic-rich diet.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.920
Once upon a time, fiber
was just thought of as just

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:55.280
the undigested component
of foods, known only for

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.040
bulking up stools and
keeping our bowels regular.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.080
Then, we discovered an array
of receptors in the body in which

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.080
fiber breakdown products
fit in like a lock-and-key.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.720
We feed our good bacteria
with fiber, and they feed us

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.520
right back, munching the fiber
and creating short chain

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:14.000
fatty acids that get absorbed
into our bloodstream and

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.360
fit into these receptors that
are expressed on immune cells

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.120
and generally mediate a direct
anti-inﬂammatory effect.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.680
So, the reason for lower
systemic inﬂammation in

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.240
plant-based eaters may not
just be due to the abundance

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.600
of anti-inﬂammatory molecules
in plant foods or the

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:33.440
avoidance of proinﬂammatory
molecules in animal foods,

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:36.000
but from the production of
anti-inflammatory molecules

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.640
from scratch by our good gut
bugs when we feed them fiber.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.360
Just to give you an idea how
protective fiber-rich foods

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:46.560
can be, those randomized to
get advice to eat fiber-rich

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.920
plant foods during radiation
therapy for cancer didn’t just

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.720
experience reduced toxicity
during the treatments,

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.680
but even a full year later.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.320
Indeed, the benefits of fiber are supported

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.400
by more than a century of research.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.040
Prospective studies show
striking reductions in death

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.880
from all causes put together,
including “total cancer deaths,

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:09.680
total cardiovascular disease
deaths and incidence,

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.400
stroke incidence, and
incidence of colorectal,

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.560
breast, and esophageal cancer.”

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.360
And “dose-response
relationships” suggest that

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.320
the more the better, in
terms of protecting against

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.280
heart attacks and stroke,
type 2 diabetes, and cancer.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.560
So, at a minimum, fiber
intakes should be no less than

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.600
25–29 grams per day,with additional benefits

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.280
likely to accrue with higher intakes.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.400
Yet, the average American only consumes

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.680
about 16 grams of ﬁber per day.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.800
We have coevolved over
millennia with gut bacteria

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.360
to the point of reliance
on our good gut bugs,

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:46.560
a kind of symbiosis for
ﬁber digestion and

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.320
the production of short chain fatty acids,

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.240
and even certain vitamins.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:53.360
Yet, we’re not holding up
our end of the bargain.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.960
We’re supposed to be providing up
to 100 or so grams of fiber a day,

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:01.040
and we are barely passing
along a measly 16 grams.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.800
The simplest solution, the
simplest approach to remedy this

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.160
lack of dietary fiber is
to encourage consumption

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.214
of whole food plant-based nutrition.

